Origin: DHI
Description: Mark the non-security MD5 uses of the API as usedforsecurity=False.
 The report storage path hash, the GraphQL hashedPath resolvers and the
 gravatar/avatars.io avatar URLs use MD5 as a cheap obfuscation hash, not as a
 security control. Under the OpenSSL FIPS provider hashlib.md5() raises
 UnsupportedDigestmodError unless the call is marked usedforsecurity=False, so
 these call sites fail on the -fips variants. usedforsecurity is accepted by
 every Python this package builds against (3.9+); the digests are unchanged.
Forwarded: not-yet
Upstream: https://github.com/codecov/umbrella (tag self-hosted-26.7.6)
diff --git a/apps/codecov-api/graphql_api/types/file/file.py b/apps/codecov-api/graphql_api/types/file/file.py
index eccb9cf6f..59ee8516c 100644
--- a/apps/codecov-api/graphql_api/types/file/file.py
+++ b/apps/codecov-api/graphql_api/types/file/file.py
@@ -48,6 +48,6 @@ def resolve_totals(data, info):
 def resolve_hashed_path(data, info):
     path = data.get("path")
     encoded_path = path.encode()
-    md5_path = hashlib.md5(encoded_path)
+    md5_path = hashlib.md5(encoded_path, usedforsecurity=False)
 
     return md5_path.hexdigest()
